.\" ABSD manual page source (mdoc(7)); rendered by scripts/render-man.sh.
.Dd September 27, 2026
.Dt UPTIME 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm uptime
.Nd how long this boot has run, and which boot it is
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints one line:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
up 0 days 00:12:34, 754434 ticks since boot, boot 3f2a...
.Ed
.Pp
The time is counted by the kernel's boot tick counter: timer interrupts
since the kernel started, about 1000.15 a second
.Pq PIT channel 0 .
It restarts at zero every boot and never goes back within one.
It counts interrupts delivered, so under emulation it can run slower than
real time; it is not the real-time clock
.Pq Xr date 1 .
.Pp
The boot is the kernel's boot identity: 16 bytes, shown in hexadecimal,
drawn once when the kernel starts and never the same for two boots.
The file server writes it into
.Pa /var/log/fsd
when it starts, so a log line can be matched to its boot.
.Pp
There is no load average and no count of users or sessions; see
.Xr ps 1
for this session's processes.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0, or 2 when given any argument.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr date 1 ,
.Xr ps 1 ,
.Xr afterboot 8
